// Formatting macros: build a String from text and values that implement Show.
//
//     name = String::from "rock"
//     s = %format "Hello ", name, ", you are ", 42
//     %println "Hello ", name, "!"
//
// Each argument is turned into a String with `show` and the results are joined
// in order. `show` borrows its receiver, so arguments stay usable afterwards.
// A call takes the rest of its line; wrap it in parentheses to use the result
// inside a larger expression, and wrap calls that take arguments, as in
// `"sum: ", (add 1, 2)`.

< macro format
    $first:expr $( , $rest:expr )* =>
        ($first).show! $( .concat (($rest).show!) )*

< macro println
    $first:expr $( , $rest:expr )* =>
        (%format $first $( , $rest )*).println!
